  <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"><i>Merger&#160;and&#160;integration&#160;expense</i></p>
  <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
  <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify;">Merger and integration expenses for the three months ended&#160;June 30, 2026&#160;increase&#160;by $3.3&#160;million, to $3.6&#160;million as compared to $0.3 million for the three months ended&#160;March 31, 2026. The increase was primarily due to professional cost incurred in connection with acquisition of Enhanced Drilling and legal cost related to the Redomicile.</p>
  <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
  <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"><i>Stock-based compensation expense</i></p>
  <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>
  <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify;">Stock-based compensation expense&#160;for the three months ended&#160;June 30, 2026&#160;increased by $2.3 million or 31.4%, to $9.6 million as compared to $7.3 million for the three months ended&#160;March 31, 2026. The increase was primarily attributable&#160;to&#160;stock-based compensation awarded in the annual LTIP grant cycle&#160;which contributed to higher expenses in the second quarter of 2026.</p>
